Week 7 — Security Audit and System Evaluation
← Week 6 | Week 7 →
Overview
Week 7 focuses on conducting a comprehensive security audit and evaluating the overall system configuration. This phase consolidates all prior work, ensuring that security controls, performance optimisations, and remote administration practices are fully documented and verified.
Objectives
Perform system security scanning and network assessment
Verify mandatory access controls and firewall configurations
Audit running services and justify their necessity
Document remaining risks and remediation strategies
Produce final reflections and lessons learned
Security Audit
Tools Used:
Lynis: Security auditing tool
nmap: Network scanning for open ports
AppArmor/SELinux status checks
fail2ban logs
User and service audit commands
Lynis Audit
sudo lynis audit system
Initial scan score: 65/100
Remediations applied: SSH hardening, firewall rules, AppArmor enforcement, fail2ban configuration
Final scan score: 85/100
Evidence:
Screenshot showing before/after Lynis scores
Network Security Assessment
nmap -sS -p 1-1024 192.168.56.103
Only SSH port (22) was open and accessible from the workstation
All other ports blocked by UFW firewall
Evidence:
nmap scan screenshot confirming restricted access
Access Control Verification
Verified AppArmor profiles are in enforce mode
Confirmed non-root administrative user has appropriate sudo privileges
Root login remains disabled
Evidence:
aa-status screenshot
sudo -l -U adminuser output
Service Audit
Checked running services using:
systemctl list-units --type=service --state=running
Only essential services running: ssh, nginx, ufw, apparmor, fail2ban
Unnecessary services stopped and disabled
Remaining Risks
Risk	Mitigation	Status
Outdated optional packages	Regular updates via unattended-upgrades	Mitigated
Insider threat on admin user	Enforced strong passwords and sudo auditing	Partially mitigated
Network exposure if firewall misconfigured	Restricted host-only network	Mitigated
System Evaluation
Security hardening successfully applied (SSH, firewall, AppArmor, fail2ban)
Performance optimisations improved CPU and disk I/O efficiency
Remote administration via SSH confirmed
Monitoring scripts functional for ongoing system metrics collection
Learning Outcome Alignment
LO3: Security vulnerabilities identified and mitigated
LO4: Proficiency in CLI administration demonstrated
LO5: Critical evaluation of system trade-offs completed
Reflection (Week 7)
Week 7 consolidates security, performance, and remote management skills. Conducting a full security audit highlighted the importance of continuous monitoring and layered defense. Performance analysis combined with security hardening reinforced the balance between security and efficiency.
This week also demonstrated the importance of documenting processes and evidence, enabling reproducibility and verification in professional settings.
